==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*fleuganą}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|ang|fleogan|flēoġan}} (Modern {{cog|en|fly}}), {{cog|ofs|fliaga|fliāga}} ({{cog|stq|fljooge}}), {{cog|osx|fliogan}} ({{cog|nds|flegen}}), {{cog|odt|fliogan}} ({{cog|nl|vliegen}}), {{cog|goh|fliogan}} ({{cog|de|fliegen}}). Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*plewk-}}. Indo-European cognates include {{cog|lt|plaukti|plaũkti}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|flaug|flugu|floginn}}

# to [[fly]]

====Conjugation====
Having a final '''''-g''''', the past indicative singular form may be {{m|non|fló}} instead of the otherwise regular {{m|non|flaug}}. In the second person, the final '''''-t''''' is geminated so that ''fló'' + ''-t'' = ''flótt''.
{{non-conj-strong|class=2|fljúg|1i=flýg|flaug|2g=fló|flug|3i=flyg|flog}}

